        "id": "dd-2026-09-06-05",
        "subject": "chemistry",
        "chapter": "Chemical Equilibrium",
        "difficulty": "easy",
        "type": "mcq",
        "question": {
          "en": "What is the relation between $K_p$ and $K_c$ for the reaction $\\text{N}_2(g) + 3\\text{H}_2(g) \\rightleftharpoons 2\\text{NH}_3(g)$?",
          "hi": "अभिक्रिया $\\text{N}_2(g) + 3\\text{H}_2(g) \\rightleftharpoons 2\\text{NH}_3(g)$ के लिए $K_p$ और $K_c$ में क्या संबंध है?"
        },
        "options": [
          {"id": "A", "text": {"en": "$K_p = K_c (RT)^{-2}$", "hi": "$K_p = K_c (RT)^{-2}$"}},
          {"id": "B", "text": {"en": "$K_p = K_c (RT)^{2}$", "hi": "$K_p = K_c (RT)^{2}$"}},
          {"id": "C", "text": {"en": "$K_p = K_c$", "hi": "$K_p = K_c$"}},
          {"id": "D", "text": {"en": "$K_p = K_c (RT)^{-1}$", "hi": "$K_p = K_c (RT)^{-1}$"}}
        ],
        "correctAnswer": "A",
        "solution": {
          "en": "$\\Delta n_g = 2 - (1 + 3) = -2$. $K_p = K_c (RT)^{\\Delta n_g} = K_c (RT)^{-2}$.",
          "hi": "$\\Delta n_g = 2 - (1 + 3) = -2$। $K_p = K_c (RT)^{\\Delta n_g} = K_c (RT)^{-2}$।"
        }
      },
